+/*
+ * T8020 has no registers of its own: it reuses the S5L8960X layout above.
+ *
+ * This was first written against the ADT, which lists /arm-io/usb-complex
+ * usb_widget_with_mask as three (offset, value, mask) triplets at 0x28, 0x38
+ * and 0x48, value 0x88, mask 0x030000ff, matching the T8011 bit layout. That
+ * reading is wrong. With it the PHY comes up and a host sees the attach and
+ * the high speed chirp, but the DMA remap is never programmed, so every
+ * control transfer times out with "device descriptor read/64, error -110".
+ *
+ * PongoOS is the reference that settles it: it gives 0x8011 and 0x8015
+ * explicit cases and lets everything else, A12 included, fall through to the
+ * S5L8960X path. Its gadget works on this phone.
+ */
+
